  "selected": [
    {
      "id": "cmip6-mlotst-definition",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-mlotst-definition.md",
      "sha256": "7c9f821afb300a640b26dbd03993d309a09793518640191dc82d641f6a4f5cb5",
      "reason": "Gives the exact criterion (surface-referenced ΔB = 0.0003 m s-2 / Δρ ≈ 0.03 kg m-3 at local pressure, computed online each time step then monthly-averaged) that the offline operator MLD must reproduce, so it fixes the threshold, the sign/direction of the crossing and the reference level.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Operator criterion: displaced surface parcel compared at local pressure, δB = −g(ρ_displaced − ρ_local)/ρ_local; MLD = first depth where δB > ΔB_crit = 0.0003 m s-2 (Δρ_crit = 0.03 kg m-3), interpolated between the bracketing levels; not the KPP boundary-layer depth.",
        "Pass `ref_depth` = the model's shallowest level to `compute_mixed_layer_depth`; exclude columns where the threshold is never reached (GFDL/MPI fill roughly full column, CESM2 often 0 m) and report that excluded area; the operator is expected shallower than `mlotst`, so state the three differences (reference level, displaced-parcel vs σ0, time averaging) instead of calling the residual model error."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "mlotst is a monthly average of an online nonlinear diagnostic while the operator is computed from monthly-mean thetao/so, so exact agreement is not expected; this caveat must be stated and bounds the internal-consistency ranking.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "f(monthly mean) ≠ monthly mean of f: compute the MLD of each March/September profile first, then average over the 30 instances; the MLD of an averaged profile is systematically shallower.",
        "Averaging the 30 monthly means of one calendar month is a plain mean over years, with no day weights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "Fixes the requirement of one mask (cells where both fields are defined in all 30 Marches/Septembers) applied to both fields, and allows the three models to be ranked only over cells all of them cover, which is exactly the requested comparison/ranking design.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Build one shared mask for the two fields with `build_comparison_mask` (`ocean_only=False`, since WOA23 is not in this comparison) and apply it with `.where(mask)` before any metric; report the retained cell/area counts beside the metrics."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-thetao-potential-temperature.md",
      "sha256": "cf8b1424a04be2e18362300d2e76d09e3f958f9d6a451c733a0cf9938968e73c",
      "reason": "The operator density must be formed from thetao as potential temperature (reference 0 dbar) plus local pressure, not from in-situ temperature, otherwise the crossing depth is biased.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`thetao` is potential temperature referenced to the ocean surface: in TEOS-10 density calculations use the potential-temperature route read by `temperature_kind()`, never the in-situ route."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-so-practical-salinity",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-so-practical-salinity.md",
      "sha256": "96f2763290996040d675ca6e8f997ea29fa320b8f6e6793bf2c6fcb739345e19",
      "reason": "Density needs Absolute Salinity derived from the practical salinity stored in `so`; treating it asAbsolute Salinity directly would shift the density criterion and the MLD.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "`so` approximates Practical Salinity with units \"0.001\": stored numbers are already of order 35, so apply no ×0.001 or ×1000; convert S_P to S_A before calling gsw density routines."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "The requested area percentages and the surface MLD statistics must be weighted with each model's areacello over all ocean cells rather than computed as unweighted cell counts.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The >20 m percentage and the covered-area percentage are shares of area, not of cells: use `compute_exceedance_fraction`, which keeps missing cells out of the denominator and returns the area behind the percentage.",
        "Area-weight every map statistic: `compute_difference_metrics` is area-weighted by default, `analyze_correlation` needs `weighting='area'`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-grid-labels",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "datasets/cmip6-grid-labels.md",
      "sha256": "e349f9e305621b6c10b35cccd0490da521cc7e3ba08bfb53890479f81024d117",
      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are native curvilinear gn grids while GFDL-ESM4 is already conservatively regridded (gr 1°×1°), which changes masks and which operations are exact for each panel/model.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr` (regridded to 1°, 35 z levels from 75 hybrid layers) while CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR are `gn`; state each model's grid when quoting numbers."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-native-grid-vs-regridded",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-native-grid-vs-regridded.md",
      "sha256": "8ff046ffbadc5794fcd2f8fe93d3bb947c736dec650aa3a3cd6e2412b7da8e68",
      "reason": "Justifies computing the MLD and the difference fields on each model's native grid and regridding to a regular longitude-latitude frame only for the Figure 1 maps/pattern comparison, since conservative regridding alters masks and conservation.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute the bias, RMSD and correlation on each model's own grid with its own `areacello`, and regrid to a regular longitude-latitude grid for the Figure 1 maps only, stating the method ('conservative' going coarser; 'bilinear' / 'nearest_s2d' fallbacks)."
      ]
    }
